 "title": "Rockstar could have made GTA 5.5 faster. It chose 13 years instead",
 "audio": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3Lh3gaSoJDsjYAzqFyj65XamsxE/hf_20261117_053408_714086e8-4514-4290-bcbe-e947e81cdd95.wav",
 "script": "Rockstar says it could have made GTA 5.5 and shipped it faster. It chose 13 years instead. Rockstar told The Guardian the team wanted a big swing, not more of the same. The studio has worked on GTA 6 since 2015, and the team is four times bigger than on GTA 5. Independent estimates say it cost over a billion dollars, but Rockstar won't confirm that. GTA 5 sold 230 million copies. So was the wait worth it, or should Rockstar have played it safe? Comment your pick.",
